-- A `distinct` set in a reference cycle. Well-founded (the `Nat` arm bottoms
-- out) and shape-recognized, so this must reach the same "recursive-set
-- support isn't implemented yet" diagnostic an `alias` cycle does.
--
-- `set_kind`'s `Var` arm recurses into a `DefKind::Distinct` def's basis
-- (via `kind::named_union_value_kind`), so a distinct def in a cycle
-- stack-overflows the compiler unless `wellfounded::build_raw_dep_graph`
-- gives it an edge — see the doc comment there.
T = distinct (Nat | T * T)

f : Int -> Int
f(x) = x
